('113.44.d.13.A',3,'Paying taxes is an example of what?','["a punishment", "an optional gift", "a right only for citizens", "a civic obligation"]'::jsonb,3,'Taxes fund public services.','original'),
('113.44.d.13.B',3,'Which is a duty of citizens?','["obeying laws", "running for office", "voting", "attending rallies"]'::jsonb,0,'Laws must be obeyed by all.','original'),
('113.44.d.13.B',3,'Which is a responsibility rather than a legal duty?','["obeying laws", "voting", "paying taxes", "serving on a jury"]'::jsonb,1,'Voting is voluntary.','original'),
('113.44.d.13.C',3,'To vote in a U.S. election, a person must be at least how old?','["21", "25", "18", "16"]'::jsonb,2,'The 26th Amendment set the voting age.','original'),
('113.44.d.13.C',3,'A person must be a U.S. citizen and what else to vote?','["a college graduate", "a property owner", "a taxpayer only", "registered to vote"]'::jsonb,3,'Most states require registration before voting.','original'),
('113.44.d.14.A',3,'Which is an effective method of political participation?','["contacting elected officials", "ignoring elections", "avoiding the news", "hiding opinions"]'::jsonb,0,'Citizens have many ways to engage.','original'),
('113.44.d.14.A',3,'A petition is used to do what?','["rewrite the Constitution", "ask government to take an action", "ban newspapers", "declare war"]'::jsonb,1,'The First Amendment protects it.','original'),
('113.44.d.14.B',3,'The women''s suffrage movement worked to win what?','["an end to child labor", "an eight-hour workday", "the right of women to vote", "free public schools"]'::jsonb,2,'The 19th Amendment passed in 1920.','original'),
('113.44.d.14.B',3,'The Montgomery bus boycott (1955-56) was an example of what?','["a military coup", "a violent revolt", "a government program", "a citizen movement using nonviolent protest"]'::jsonb,3,'It helped launch the modern civil rights movement.','original'),
('113.44.d.14.C',3,'Which factor most influences a person''s political attitudes?','["family and peers", "the tides", "the number of planets", "the length of day"]'::jsonb,0,'Socialization shapes views.','original'),
('113.44.d.14.C',3,'The media influence political attitudes by doing what?','["enforcing laws", "shaping what issues people see and how they see them", "writing laws", "counting votes"]'::jsonb,1,'News coverage frames issues.','original'),
('113.44.d.15.A',3,'An interest group is organized to do what?','["run schools", "nominate presidents", "influence government policy on specific issues", "decide court cases"]'::jsonb,2,'Examples include the NRA and AARP.','original'),
('113.44.d.15.A',3,'Political action committees (PACs) raise money to do what?','["draw district lines", "count votes", "enforce laws", "support candidates or causes"]'::jsonb,3,'Their spending is regulated.','original'),
('113.44.d.15.B',3,'The right of petition allows citizens to do what?','["ask government to correct grievances", "break any law", "ignore courts", "avoid taxes"]'::jsonb,0,'It is part of the First Amendment.','original'),
('113.44.d.15.B',3,'Which kind of speech is NOT protected by the First Amendment?','["unpopular political opinions", "speech that incites imminent lawless action", "criticism of the government", "peaceful protest"]'::jsonb,1,'The Court allows limits on dangerous speech.','original'),
('113.44.d.16.A',3,'The Civil Rights Act of 1964 banned what?','["private clubs", "public schools", "discrimination based on race, color, religion, sex or national origin", "voting by mail"]'::jsonb,2,'It outlawed segregation in public places.','original'),
('113.44.d.16.B',3,'The Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 prohibits what?','["voting by mail", "all disability benefits", "private school", "discrimination against people with disabilities"]'::jsonb,3,'It requires accessibility.','original'),
('113.44.d.16.B',3,'The 26th Amendment changed American politics by doing what?','["lowering the voting age to 18", "giving women the vote", "creating term limits", "ending poll taxes"]'::jsonb,0,'It passed in 1971.','original'),
('113.44.d.17.A',3,'A patent protects an inventor by doing what?','["ending competition", "giving the exclusive right to make and sell the invention for a period", "making inventions free", "banning new inventions"]'::jsonb,1,'The Constitution authorizes patents to promote progress.','original'),
('113.44.d.17.A',3,'The Constitution allows Congress to grant patents and copyrights to do what?','["tax inventors only", "limit all ideas", "promote science and the useful arts", "control newspapers"]'::jsonb,2,'Intellectual property fosters innovation.','original'),
('113.44.d.17.B',3,'The Internet began as a government project funded by which agency?','["the Postal Service", "NASA", "the Treasury", "ARPA (a Defense Department research agency)"]'::jsonb,3,'ARPANET became the basis of the Internet.','original'),
('113.44.d.17.B',3,'GPS technology was developed with government support for what use?','["military navigation, later shared with private industry", "city planning only", "farm subsidies", "education"]'::jsonb,0,'Public research can yield private benefits.','original'),
('113.44.d.18.A',3,'Advances in biotechnology raise policy questions about what?','["only sports", "ethics, safety and regulation", "only fashion", "only weather"]'::jsonb,1,'Government must balance innovation and risk.','original'),
('113.44.d.18.A',3,'Government regulation of drones is an example of what?','["repealing the Constitution", "banning all travel", "adapting laws to new technology", "ending technology"]'::jsonb,2,'New tools prompt new rules.','original'),
('113.44.d.18.B',3,'How has the Internet changed political campaigns?','["it ended debates", "it banned campaigns", "it ended voting", "it allows candidates to reach voters and raise money quickly"]'::jsonb,3,'Digital media is central to campaigns.','original'),
('113.44.d.18.B',3,'A risk of social media in politics is what?','["the rapid spread of misinformation", "fewer opinions", "no communication", "no engagement"]'::jsonb,0,'Citizens must evaluate sources.','original'),
('113.44.d.19.A',3,'Putting the steps of a bill becoming a law in order is an example of what?','["memorizing dates", "sequencing information", "averaging data", "ignoring causes"]'::jsonb,1,'Analysis includes sequencing.','original'),
('113.44.d.19.B',3,'A good product on a government issue should be based on what?','["one opinion", "unsourced posts", "credible evidence and clear reasoning", "rumors"]'::jsonb,2,'Critical methods strengthen products.','original'),
('113.44.d.19.C',3,'To defend a point of view on a political issue, a student should do what?','["ignore other views", "shout louder", "use no facts", "support it with evidence and address counterarguments"]'::jsonb,3,'Strong arguments consider opposing views.','original'),
('113.44.d.19.D',3,'To judge a source''s validity, a student should ask what?','["who wrote it, why, and what evidence it uses", "what color it is", "how many ads it has", "how long it is"]'::jsonb,0,'Credibility depends on the author and evidence.','original'),
('113.44.d.19.D',3,'A source that clearly favors one side is said to show what?','["neutrality", "bias", "fact", "objectivity"]'::jsonb,1,'Bias shapes how information is presented.','original'),
('113.44.d.19.E',3,'A bar graph of voter turnout by age group helps show what?','["the date of elections", "the number of senators", "which groups vote at higher or lower rates", "the weather"]'::jsonb,2,'Charts help evaluate government data.','original'),
('113.44.d.19.F',3,'A claim in a civics essay should be supported by what?','["guesses", "assumptions", "opinions only", "evidence and reasoning"]'::jsonb,3,'Evidence supports claims.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Social Studies' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'hs_gov_v1'
from (values
('113.44.d.20.A',3,'Using the term ''bicameral'' correctly describes what kind of legislature?','["one with two chambers", "one without elections", "one with one chamber", "one led by a king"]'::jsonb,0,'Congress is bicameral.','original'),
('113.44.d.20.A',3,'A ''bill'' is best defined as what?','["an election result", "a proposed law", "a tax return", "a court order"]'::jsonb,1,'A bill must pass both houses.','original'),
('113.44.d.20.B',3,'An effective presentation about a government issue should include what?','["only opinions", "only pictures", "a clear thesis, evidence and a logical order", "no sources"]'::jsonb,2,'Organization and evidence make it effective.','original'),
('113.44.d.20.C',3,'Civil discourse in a political discussion means what?','["insulting those who disagree", "refusing to listen", "spreading rumors", "respectful exchange of ideas supported by evidence"]'::jsonb,3,'Respect and evidence guide discussion.','original'),
('113.44.d.21.A',3,'A jury trial is an example of what democratic process?','["citizens taking part in justice", "a vote for president", "a primary election", "a tax audit"]'::jsonb,0,'Jurors decide cases.','original'),
('113.44.d.21.B',3,'A class has defined a local civic problem and collected facts. What should they do before choosing a solution?','["wait for someone else to decide", "list and weigh the possible options", "ignore the facts they collected", "end the project"]'::jsonb,1,'Evaluate options before choosing.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Social Studies' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
